neline|head -2; git diff ac40f7c HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-900"]], "output": "```console\n9365073 Brief rev. 6: align with pre-registration\nac40f7c Brief rev. 5: floor, eligibility, minimum cells in T\n--- a/Brief.md\n+++ b/Brief.md\n-# Brief — the idea (rev. 5: floor, eligibility and minimum cells on the common target set)\n+# Brief — the idea (rev. 6: aligned with the experiment-repo pre-registration)\n-- **Margin aggregation:** δ_j per benchmark as above (training data); the pooled verdict for a model uses the pooled RMSE over T, and the pooled margin is δ_T = sqrt(mean_{j∈T} δ_j²) (same aggregation as the error); the verdict is computed on that pooled difference and δ_T averaged over splits. Per-benchmark verdicts are secondary.\n+- **Margin aggregation:** δ_j per benchmark as above (training data); the pooled verdict for a model uses the pooled RMSE over T, and the pooled margin is δ = the mean of δ_j over the evaluated target cells (as fixed in `experiment-repo` `prereg/PREREG.md` F; supersedes my earlier root-mean-square form; the headline error is the mean over held-out models of model RMSE, so a mean margin is on the same footing); the verdict is computed on that pooled difference and δ_T averaged over splits. Per-benchmark verdicts are secondary.\n+\n+**Accepted from the pre-registration (experiment-repo `prereg/PREREG.md`, commit 7731e49):** realised MTEB matrix 238 models × 328 tasks, 83 org groups, grid up to k=109=⌊N/3⌋ (|C|≈2N/3, k ≤ ⌊|C|/2⌋); **k\\*(ε) defined on the excess over the model's own all-others floor on the same targets** (since δ ≤ 0.25·floor, absolute error ≤ δ is unreachable) with ε ∈ {δ, 2δ}; baseline adaptations stay in the comparison and are labelled as adaptations in the paper (S3 k ≤ 32, S4 on the EM-completed matrix, S7 continuous kNN/tree interview, P2 on EM-completed training matrix, **P6 = PC regression on the P5 latent scores with a sigmoid link, \"adapted from Ruan et al./Sloth\", never \"as published\"**); S8 exhaustive oracle only on N ≤ 10 matrices plus greedy-vs-exhaustive on small random MTEB subsets. N=328 is large because MTEB tasks are fine-grained (117 retrieval tasks):\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "52a8cf21-8486-5809-9ba6-0fd12f0b3d5f", "at": 1795729645.6372638, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 14727, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "c83ccfe82438f8f46876e84186bcaf48", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "aa806820-0b6b-5369-8c2f-3f47104622a6", "at": 1795729645.6414473, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 14728, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "c83ccfe82438f8f46876e84186bcaf48", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "c3a3c9b7-56fb-50ab-8004-a6f8094559a7", "at": 1795729645.6447494, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 14729, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "c83ccfe82438f8f46876e84186bcaf48", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "aa6b8efd-0bd9-5baf-837e-a473a97514c9", "at": 1795729645.711479, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 14730, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "c83ccfe82438f8f46876e84186bcaf48", "trust": "system-confirmed", 